    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: panicle-like/paniculiform: 443 statements in 16 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of PATO:0002455 corymb-like. 2026-11-14: parent PATO:0000052 -> PATO:0000141; definition reworded after the second-model review of the definitions (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "paniculiform"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991199 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "thyrse-like"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's branching pattern resembling a thyrse, an inflorescence with an indeterminate main axis and cymose lateral branches."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: thyrse-like/thyrsoid/thyrsiform: 171 statements in 19 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of PATO:0002455 corymb-like. 2026-11-14: parent PATO:0000052 -> PATO:0000141; definition reworded after the second-model review of the definitions (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "thyrsiform"^^xsd:string,
        "thyrsoid"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991200 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "bract-like"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being reduced, small and leaf-like or scale-like, resembling a bract."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: bract-like/bracteiform: 93 statements in 18 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of PATO:0002459 sepal-like. 2026-11-14: definition reworded after the second-model review of the definitions (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "bracteiform"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991202 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "triplinerved"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having three main veins, the two lateral ones arising from the midvein above the base."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000402 (branched), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: triplinerved: 63 statements in 11 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)"@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000402 .

obo:FLOPO_0991203 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "alveolate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's surface being marked with close-set angular depressions like a honeycomb."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000150 (texture), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: alveolate/honeycombed: 224 statements in 15 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of PATO:0002296 foveate (scattered pits)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "honeycombed"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000150 .

obo:FLOPO_0991204 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "scalariform"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A spatial pattern quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's parts, such as veins, bars, pits or thickenings, being arranged in parallel transverse rows like the rungs of a ladder."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000060 (spatial pattern), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: scalariform/ladder-like: 307 statements in 11 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2) 2026-11-14: definition reworded after the second-model review of the definitions (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "ladder-like"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000060 .

obo:FLOPO_0991205 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ruminate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being irregularly furrowed and infolded, often by ingrowths of a surrounding layer such as the seed coat, so that its surface or cut face looks mottled, as if chewed."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000150 (texture), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: ruminate: 96 statements in 14 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2) 2026-11-14: definition reworded after the second-model review of the definitions (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000150 .

obo:FLOPO_0991206 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "streaked"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A multi-colored quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being marked with narrow, irregular lines of a different colour."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001533 (multi-colored), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: streaked: 285 statements in 19 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of PATO:0001946 banded and PATO:0000333 spotted."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001533 .

obo:FLOPO_0991207 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "descending"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An oblique orientation quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being directed obliquely downward."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002481 (oblique orientation), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: descending: 152 statements in 17 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling and opposite of PATO:0104355 ascending."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002481 .

obo:FLOPO_0991208 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "marginal"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A peripheral quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being located at or on the margin of the flattened structure that bears it."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002107 (peripheral), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: marginal: 136 statements in 16 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). With PATO:0002476 terminal and PATO:0002107 peripheral. 2026-11-14: parent PATO:0000140 -> PATO:0002107; definition reworded after the second-model review of the definitions (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002107 .

obo:FLOPO_0991209 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "barbed"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's bearing short, stiff, sharp projections (barbs) that point back towards its base, like the barbs of a fish-hook or arrow-head."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: barbed/glochidiate: 409 statements in 18 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2) 2026-11-14: definition reworded after the second-model review of the definitions (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "glochidiate"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991210 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "spine-tipped"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A pointed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ending in a spine."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002258 (pointed), added 2026-11-13 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: spine-tipped/spinose-tipped/spine tipped: 218 statements in 19 floras (staged candidates 2026-11-13)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-13: added in the flora candidate review, batch 2 (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)"@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002258 .

obo:FLOPO_0991212 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "monomorphic"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A morphological quality inhering in a set of homologous plant structures by virtue of its members occurring in a single form."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000051 (morphology), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: homomorphic/monomorphic: 616 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling and opposite of FLOPO:0991092 dimorphic; 'not dimorphic' would also cover trimorphic sets."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "isomorphic"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000051 .

obo:FLOPO_0991213 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "margined"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's having a distinct marginal band that differs from the rest of it in colour, texture, thickness or cell form."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: limbate/marginate/margined/rimmed/unbordered: 600 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Covers narrowly margined seeds and bracts and the bordered (limbidiate) leaves of mosses; the band itself is a plant organ margin (PO:0025005)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "bordered"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991214 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "wiry"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being slender, tough and resilient, like wire."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000150 (texture), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: wiry: 539 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991126 corky; combines slenderness with toughness, which PATO:0001545 inflexible does not."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000150 .

obo:FLOPO_0991215 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "callose"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's bearing hard, thickened, often pale spots or tips (calluses)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000150 (texture), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: callose/callous/calloused: 411 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Not the polysaccharide callose; 'callus' was rejected as a generic part, so this cannot be a presence rule."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "calleux"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000150 .

obo:FLOPO_0991216 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "appendiculate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's bearing one or more small outgrowths or appendages."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: appendiculate: 351 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991029 horned and FLOPO:0991196 crested; the appendages of anthers, petals and peristome cilia have different origins, so no part is named."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "appendaged"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991217 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mammillate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's bearing one or more nipple-shaped protuberances, broader and blunter than papillae."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: mamillose/mammillate/mammillose: 316 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991059 papillose; in mosses a mammilla is a bulge of the whole cell wall, a papilla a solid outgrowth. PATO:0002108 papillary is the bearer's itself resembling a nipple."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "mamillate"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991218 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "flat-topped"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's upper surface or outline being more or less level, its distal parts reaching about the same height."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: flat topped/flattopped: 313 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). PATO:0002455 corymb-like is the inflorescence architecture; flat-topped cymes, panicles, fruits and moss lamella cells are not corymbs."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991219 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "turgid"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being swollen and full, rounded in section rather than flattened, as if filled with fluid."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: tumid/turgid: 307 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Not PATO:0001851 swollen or PATO:0001602 distended (abnormal), PATO:0002376 inflated (air-filled) or PATO:0001622 increased turgor (cell pressure)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "plump"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991220 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "homogamous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A phenotypic sex quality inhering in an inflorescence by virtue of the bearer's containing flowers of only one sexual kind, such as a capitulum of all bisexual flowers."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001894 (phenotypic sex), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: homogamous: 305 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Opposite of FLOPO:0991178 heterogamous. The pollination sense (anthers and stigmas maturing together, 'flowers homogamous') is a different quality and is not covered. 2026-11-15: parent PATO:0000141 -> PATO:0001894; definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "homogame"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001894 .

obo:FLOPO_0991221 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "doubly serrate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A serrated quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's marginal teeth bearing smaller teeth on their own margins."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001206 (serrated), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: biserrate/biserrulate/double serrate/doubly serrate: 283 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Child of PATO:0001206 serrated; sibling of FLOPO:0991081 serrulate."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "duplicate-serrate"^^xsd:string,
        "duplicato-serrate"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001206 .

obo:FLOPO_0991222 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "spathaceous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a spathe: large, sheathing and enclosing, often split down one side."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: spathaceous/spathe like/spathelike/spathiform: 255 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991200 bract-like; a bract that is itself a spathe is the bearer FLOPO_0986007 spathe."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "spathacé"^^xsd:string,
        "spathiforme"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991223 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pustulate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A rough quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's surface bearing small, rounded, blister-like elevations, often at the bases of hairs."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000700 (rough), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: pustular/pustulate/pustulose: 254 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991060 tuberculate; smaller than FLOPO:0991122 bullate; not PATO:0001928 blistered, which is an accumulation of fluid. 2026-11-15: parent PATO:0000150 -> PATO:0000700; definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "pustuleux"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000700 .

obo:FLOPO_0991224 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "scapiform"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's resembling a scape: a long, leafless or nearly leafless axis arising at or near the base of the plant and bearing flowers at its tip."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: scape like/scapelike/scapiform: 244 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). 2026-11-15: definition reworded; 'scapose' is a related synonym after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "scapiforme"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "scapose"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991225 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "gynaecandrous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A phenotypic sex quality inhering in an inflorescence by virtue of its bearing both pistillate and staminate flowers on the same axis, the pistillate above the staminate."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001894 (phenotypic sex), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: gynaecandrous/gynecandrous: 218 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Child of FLOPO:0991037 androgynous, whose definition does not fix the order. In Carex usage 'androgynous' means the opposite order (staminate above), which would need a sibling class. 2026-11-15: parent FLOPO:0991037 -> PATO:0001894; definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001894 .

obo:FLOPO_0991226 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "proliferous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's producing buds, shoots or plantlets from which new plants arise vegetatively."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: proliferous: 195 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Botany-specific (includes pseudoviviparous spikelets and root-suckering roots); PATO:0002102 proliferative is a cell-division quality."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "proliferating"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991227 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "bipinnatifid"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A pinnatifid quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lobes being themselves pinnatifid, so that the bearer is twice pinnately incised."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath FLOPO:0991078 (pinnatifid), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: bipinnatifid: 193 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Follows FLOPO:0991014 bipinnate; sibling of FLOPO:0991155 pinnatisect. 2026-11-15: definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "bipennatifide"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:FLOPO_0991078 .

obo:FLOPO_0991228 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hemi-epiphytic"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A positional quality inhering in a plant by virtue of its growing as an epiphyte for part of its life and rooted in the ground for the other part, either starting on a host and sending roots down to the soil or starting in the soil and later losing its connection with it."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000140 (position), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: hemi epiphyte/hemi epiphytic/hemiepiphyte/hemiepiphytic: 191 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991110 epiphytic; not a child of it, as the plant is not always epiphytic."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000140 .

obo:FLOPO_0991229 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pandurate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A 2-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's outline being fiddle-shaped: obovate to oblong and contracted by a concave indentation on each side below the middle."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002006 (2-D shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: fiddle shaped/pandurate/panduriform/subpandurate/subpanduriform/subpanduriforme/violin shaped: 184 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991024 ovate and FLOPO:0991056 obcordate; distinct from FLOPO:0991057 lyrate, which is a lobing."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "panduriforme"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002006 .

obo:FLOPO_0991230 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "spine-like"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a spine: narrow, rigid and ending in a sharp point."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: spine like/spinelike/spiniform: 177 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991200 bract-like and FLOPO:0991143 scale-like; FLOPO:0991210 spine-tipped is a bearer that only ends in a spine. 2026-11-15: 'spinescent' is a related synonym after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "spinescent"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991231 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "fugacious"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A deciduous quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's disposition to fall very early, soon after it is formed or after the structure it subtends opens."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001730 (deciduous (generic)), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: caduceus/early withering/fugaceous/fugacious: 173 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991181 marcescent and PATO:0001731 deciduous (plant), which is the shedding of foliage. 2026-11-15: parent PATO:0001729 -> PATO:0001730; definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "early deciduous"^^xsd:string,
        "evanescent"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "caducous"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001730 .

obo:FLOPO_0991232 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "julaceous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A cylindrical quality inhering in a leafy shoot by virtue of its leaves being closely imbricate and appressed, so that the shoot is smooth, round in section and catkin-like."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001873 (cylindrical), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: julaceous: 159 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "catkin-like"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001873 .

obo:FLOPO_0991233 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "aphyllopodic"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a culm or fertile shoot by virtue of its lowest leaves being bladeless sheaths or having much reduced blades, the shoot usually arising laterally from beneath the leaves of a previous shoot."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: aphyllopodic: 150 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991234 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "parted"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A split quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being divided more than halfway, but not fully, to its base or midrib into segments."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001786 (split), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: parted: 148 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "parti"^^xsd:string,
        "partite"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001786 .

obo:FLOPO_0991235 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "glume-like"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a glume (PO:0009039): small, dry, chaffy and bract-like."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: glumaceous/glume like/glumelike/glumiform: 140 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991200 bract-like and PATO:0002459 sepal-like, worded as they are."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991236 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "obpyramidal"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A pyramidal quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being attached at the apex of the pyramid, with the polygonal base distal."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002336 (pyramidal), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: obpyramidal/obpyramidate: 139 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "inversely pyramidal"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002336 .

obo:FLOPO_0991237 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "squarrose"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A spreading quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being abruptly bent outward from an erect or appressed lower part, so that its free distal part stands out at a wide angle or recurves from the axis, as in phyllaries or moss leaves."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0104356 (spreading), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: squarrose: 138 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Child of PATO:0104356 spreading; differs from PATO:0002211 recurved in the abrupt bend near the base. 2026-11-15: definition reworded; 'squarrose-recurved' is a related synonym after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "squarrose-recurved"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0104356 .

obo:FLOPO_0991238 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "stipule-like"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a stipule."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: stipule like/stipulelike/stipuliform: 138 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991200 bract-like and PATO:0002459 sepal-like."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "resembling stipules"^^xsd:string,
        "stipuliforme"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991239 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "phyllopodic"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's lowest leaves bearing well-developed blades, the shoot usually arising from the centre of a tuft of leaves rather than laterally from beneath the leaves of a previous shoot."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: phyllopodic: 137 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). 2026-11-15: definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991240 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dolabriform"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like the head of a hatchet: narrow at the base and widening into a broad, oblique, curved distal edge."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: dolabriform/hatchet shaped: 130 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "axe-shaped"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991241 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "biternate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a compound leaf by virtue of its being divided into three primary divisions, each of which is again divided into three."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: bi ternate/biternate: 128 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "biternately compound"^^xsd:string,
        "biterné"^^xsd:string,
        "twice ternate"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991242 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "collenchymatous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being made of, or containing, collenchyma: living cells whose primary walls are unevenly thickened, usually at the corners where the cells meet."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: collenchymatous: 124 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). The bryological sense (leaf and exothecial cells); not the presence of PO:0005423 collenchyma tissue. 2026-11-15: definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "thickened at the corners"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991243 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "septate-nodulose"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being partitioned internally by transverse septa that show on the surface as small nodules or cross-ridges."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: septate nodulose: 124 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Usual in Juncus, Cyperaceae and Poaceae leaves and culms; PATO has no septate quality."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "nodulose-septate"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991244 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "colonial"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An aggregated quality inhering in a plant by virtue of its growing in a group of closely spaced shoots or individuals, usually spread vegetatively from one parent by rhizomes, stolons or root suckers."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001629 (aggregated), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: colonial: 123 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "colony-forming"^^xsd:string,
        "forming colonies"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001629 .

obo:FLOPO_0991245 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "anadromous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A spatial pattern quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the first segment or vein of each division of the bearer arising on the acroscopic side, towards the apex of the frond."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000060 (spatial pattern), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: anadromous: 121 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Fern-specific; the opposite is catadromous."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000060 .

obo:FLOPO_0991246 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pinnately branched"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A branched quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's branches arising in two rows on opposite sides of a main axis, like the barbs of a feather."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000402 (branched), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: pinnately branched: 117 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "pinnately ramified"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000402 .

obo:FLOPO_0991247 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "flagelliform"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being long, slender and flexible, tapering like a whip lash."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: flagellate/flagelliform/whip shaped: 117 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991038 virgate (straight, stiff, wand-like); PATO:0104351 filiform is thread-like and not flexible-tapering."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "whip-like"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991248 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mitrate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A concave 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like a mitre: a hollow, symmetric cone that is not split down one side, though it may be shortly lobed or split at the base on several sides."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002008 (concave 3-D shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: conic mitrate/mitrate/mitriform: 114 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling and contrast of FLOPO:0991119 cucullate (calyptra split on one side)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "mitre-shaped"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002008 .

obo:FLOPO_0991249 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hair-pointed"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A pointed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's ending in a long, slender, hair-like point, often hyaline."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002258 (pointed), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: hair pointed/piliferous: 113 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "hair-tipped"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002258 .

obo:FLOPO_0991250 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "abortive"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a plant structure by virtue of its having stopped developing before maturity, so that it is present but reduced and usually non-functional."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000588 (vestigial), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: abortive: 111 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). 2026-11-15: parent PATO:0000141 -> PATO:0000588 after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "aborted"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000588 .

obo:FLOPO_0991251 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "prorulose"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A texture quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's cells having their ends projecting as low, papilla-like protrusions (prorulae) above the surface."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000150 (texture), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: prorate/prorulose: 109 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000150 .

obo:FLOPO_0991252 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "synoicous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A phenotypic sex quality inhering in a bryophyte gametophyte by virtue of its bearing antheridia and archegonia mixed together in the same gametoecium."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001894 (phenotypic sex), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: synoicous: 104 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991093 autoicous; bryophyte sexual system, distinct from flowering-plant monoecy."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "synoecious"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001894 .

obo:FLOPO_0991253 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "excurved"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A curved quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being curved outward, away from the axis or the centre of the structure that bears it."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000406 (curved), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: excurved: 101 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). PATO:0002211 recurved (backward or inward) and PATO:0001597 everted (turned outward in placement, not curved) do not fit."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "outcurved"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000406 .

obo:FLOPO_0991254 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "tooth-like"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's similarity to the appearance of a tooth: small, short, broad-based and pointed."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000052 (shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: dentiform/tooth like/toothlike: 100 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of FLOPO:0991143 scale-like and FLOPO:0991200 bract-like, worded as they are; not PATO:0001205 dentated, which is bearing teeth."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000052 .

obo:FLOPO_0991255 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cyme-like"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's branching resembling that of a cyme, the main axis ending in a flower and later flowers arising on lateral branches below it."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: cyme like/cymiform: 99 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of PATO:0002455 corymb-like and FLOPO:0991199 thyrse-like. 2026-11-15: parent PATO:0000052 -> PATO:0000141; definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "cymoid"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "cymose"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000141 .

obo:FLOPO_0991256 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "spinose-serrate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A serrated quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's marginal teeth each ending in a spine."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001206 (serrated), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: spinose serrate: 97 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Child of PATO:0001206 serrated. Numbers before it ('5-12-spinose-serrate on each side') are a count of teeth (docs/odp/03-count-of-parts.md). 2026-11-15: 'spinulose-serrate' is a related synonym after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "spinulose-serrate"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001206 .

obo:FLOPO_0991257 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "polygonal"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A 2-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's outline or cross-section having several, usually five or more, straight sides meeting at angles."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002006 (2-D shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: irregularly polygonal/polygonal: 92 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "many-angled"^^xsd:string,
        "polygonous"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002006 .

obo:FLOPO_0991258 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "autotrophic"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A trophic quality inhering in a plant by virtue of its obtaining its carbon by its own photosynthesis, without depending on a host plant or on fungi."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000056 (trophic quality), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: autotrophic: 90 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Contrasts with mycoheterotrophic and parasitic; possibly outside PATO's scope, like FLOPO:0991110 epiphytic."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "autotrophique"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000056 .

obo:FLOPO_0991259 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "diadelphous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A connate quality inhering in an androecium or its stamens by virtue of the stamen filaments being united into two separate groups, often 9 + 1 or 5 + 5."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath FLOPO:0991067 (connate), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: diadelphous: 89 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "diadelphe"^^xsd:string,
        "diadelphic"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:FLOPO_0991067 .

obo:FLOPO_0991260 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "distylous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A heterostylous quality inhering in a flower or plant by virtue of its belonging to a species whose flowers occur in two morphs, one with long styles and short stamens and one with short styles and long stamens."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath FLOPO:0991137 (heterostylous), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: distylous: 88 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of tristylous."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "distylic"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:FLOPO_0991137 .

obo:FLOPO_0991261 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "neuter"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A sterile quality inhering in a flower by virtue of its having neither functional stamens nor a functional gynoecium."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000956 (sterile), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: neuter: 85 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). 2026-11-15: 'asexual' is a related synonym after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "asexual"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000956 .

obo:FLOPO_0991262 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "septifragal"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A dehiscent quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's opening at maturity by valves that break away from the septa, the septa remaining attached to the central axis."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath FLOPO:0991149 (dehiscent), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: septifragal/septifragous: 83 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "septifrage"^^xsd:string,
        "septifrages"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:FLOPO_0991149 .

obo:FLOPO_0991263 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "latiseptate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A flattened quality inhering in a fruit by virtue of its being compressed parallel to the septum, so that the septum lies across the broadest diameter of the fruit."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002254 (flattened), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: latiseptate: 82 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Brassicaceae silicles; the opposite is angustiseptate (compressed at right angles to the septum). Sibling of FLOPO:0991103 depressed."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002254 .

obo:FLOPO_0991264 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "chasmogamous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An open quality inhering in a flower by virtue of its opening at anthesis, so that its anthers and stigmas are exposed and it can be cross-pollinated."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000610 (open), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: chasmogamous: 79 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000610 .

obo:FLOPO_0991266 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "monocarpic"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A multi-cellular organismal disposition inhering in a plant by virtue of its flowering and fruiting only once and then dying."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001728 (multi-cellular organismal disposition), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: monocarpic: 76 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). 2026-11-15: 'hapaxanthic' is a related synonym after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "semelparous"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "hapaxanthic"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001728 .

obo:FLOPO_0991267 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "medifixed"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An attachment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being attached at or near its middle, with free arms or ends on either side of the point of attachment."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001435 (attachment quality), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: medifix/medifixed/midfix: 76 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). 2026-11-15: 'medifixed hair' is a related synonym; 'malpighian' is a related synonym after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "midfixed"^^xsd:string,
        "médifixe"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "malpighian"^^xsd:string,
        "medifixed hair"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001435 .

obo:FLOPO_0991268 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "clonal"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A multi-cellular organismal disposition inhering in a plant by virtue of its spreading vegetatively, by rhizomes, stolons, root suckers or bulbs, into a group of genetically identical shoots or ramets."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001728 (multi-cellular organismal disposition), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: clonal: 73 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Probably outside PATO's scope (how a plant grows and reproduces); kept in FLOPO beside mat-forming and caespitose. 2026-11-15: parent PATO:0000141 -> PATO:0001728; definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "clone-forming"^^xsd:string,
        "forming clones"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001728 .

obo:FLOPO_0991269 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hypogynous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A positional quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being inserted, or bearing the perianth and stamens inserted, on the receptacle below the ovary and free from it."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000140 (position), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: hypogynous: 73 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). 2026-11-15: definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000140 .

obo:FLOPO_0991270 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "palmatipartite"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A palmately lobed quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being cut palmately more than halfway, but not fully, to the base into segments radiating from a common point."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath FLOPO:0991158 (palmately lobed), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: palmately parted/palmatipartite: 72 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Palmate counterpart of FLOPO:0991156 pinnatipartite; sibling of FLOPO:0991160 pedate. 2026-11-15: parent PATO:0001786 -> FLOPO:0991158; definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "palmatiparti"^^xsd:string,
        "palmatipartit"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:FLOPO_0991158 .

obo:FLOPO_0991271 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "barrel-shaped"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A convex 3-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being shaped like a barrel: roughly cylindrical, broadest at the middle with outwardly curved sides, and truncate at both ends."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002007 (convex 3-D shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: barrel shaped: 71 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Sibling of PATO:0001873 cylindrical and FLOPO:0991120 trigonous."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "doliiform"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002007 .

obo:FLOPO_0991272 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "palmately divided"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A split quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being cut into segments that radiate from a common point, the incisions reaching more than halfway to the base."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001786 (split), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: palmately divided: 68 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Palmate counterpart of FLOPO:0991156 pinnatipartite and FLOPO:0991155 pinnatisect; deeper than FLOPO:0991158 palmately lobed; parent of FLOPO:0991160 pedate. Not PATO:0001980 digitate, which is compound."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "palmatifid"^^xsd:string,
        "palmatisect"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001786 .

obo:FLOPO_0991273 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "incumbent"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A positional quality inhering in a cotyledon by virtue of the cotyledon's back lying against the radicle, which is folded along it."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000140 (position), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: incombant/incombent/incumbent: 66 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Botany-specific (Brassicaceae); accumbent, the radicle against the cotyledon edges, is its sibling. 2026-11-15: definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "notorrhizal"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "incombant"^^xsd:string,
        "notorrhizal"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0000140 .

obo:FLOPO_0991274 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "pseudopeltate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An attachment quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's being attached just inside its basal margin, with the basal lobes overlapping so that it appears peltate."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0001435 (attachment quality), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: pseudopeltate: 66 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). Fern rhizome scales; sibling of FLOPO:0991107 peltate."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0001435 .

obo:FLOPO_0991275 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "semi-elliptic"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A 2-D shape quality inhering in a bearer by virtue of the bearer's outline being half an ellipse, bounded on one side by a straight line along one of the ellipse's axes."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0002006 (2-D shape), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: semi elliptic/semi elliptical: 65 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "half-elliptic"^^xsd:string ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:PATO_0002006 .

obo:FLOPO_0991276 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "phyllodioicous"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A dioicous quality inhering in a bryophyte gametophyte by virtue of its dwarf male plants growing epiphytically on the leaves or tomentum of the female plants."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath FLOPO:0991211 (dioicous), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: phyllodioicous/pseudautoicous/pseudoautoicous/pseudomonoicous: 65 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2). 2026-11-15: parent PATO:0001894 -> FLOPO:0991211; definition reworded after the review of the new classes (Claude Opus; checked, AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    oboInOwl:inSubset <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/pato#value_slim> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:FLOPO_0991211 .

obo:FLOPO_0991277 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "locellate"^^xsd:string ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A structural quality inhering in an anther or anther theca by virtue of its locules being divided by septa into smaller chambers (locelli)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "FLOPO-local value class beneath PATO PATO:0000141 (structure), added 2026-11-14 for quality words of the parsed flora corpora (evidence: locellate: 61 statements (second-model review 2026-11-14)). Candidate for submission to PATO. Review: 2026-11-14: proposed by the second-model review (Claude Opus) and checked (AI review, Claude Fable 5.2)."@en ;
    dcterms:date "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
